# Plico (太初) — Project Rules for Windsurf

## Overview
Rust (edition 2021) AI-native OS kernel. Semantic APIs, no human CLI/GUI.

## Commands
```bash
cargo build                                              # build
EMBEDDING_BACKEND=stub LLM_BACKEND=stub cargo test --lib # unit tests
cargo clippy -- -D warnings                              # lint
cargo fmt --check                                        # format
```

## Rules
- Files: `snake_case.rs`, < 300 lines, one concept per file
- Naming: `snake_case` fns, `PascalCase` types, `SCREAMING_SNAKE` consts
- No `#[allow(clippy::...)]` — fix issues, don't suppress
- No `unsafe` without `# Safety` comment
- Errors: `thiserror` only, no panics in lib code
- Tests: `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` inline
- Always use stub backends for tests

## Architecture
- `api/bin → kernel → tool/fs/intent → cas/memory/scheduler/temporal/llm`
- `kernel/` is the sole module importing all others
- CAS is the only module touching host filesystem
- JSON is the only kernel interface
- All persistence: `atomic_write_json()`, never `std::fs::write()`

## Security
- Reserved agents: `kernel`, `system`, `root`, `admin`
- Max content: 10 MB
- No hardcoded API keys
